<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 86,142 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 86,142 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 86,142 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Wednesday compared to 58,094 tonnes in the same period on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Tuesday     May 13</p>
<p>    Export cargo		20,192	24,929</p>
<p>    Import cargo		65,950	33,165</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, five ships sailed and eight berthed. In the next 24 hours, five are expected to sail and nine are expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	Tonnes/TEUs  Ship			Berthing</p>
<p>Crude oil	    60,000	 Capitan Miranda	 15/5</p>
<p>High speed diesel  70,000	 Sea Islecity	    15/5</p>
<p>Fuel oil	     26,246	 Atlas		     Due</p>
<p>Soyabean oil	  7,000	 Patty Anne		Due</p>
<p>Vegoil		 18,000	 Ariston		   21/5</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
